{"version":"0.12.21","prev_tag":"v0.12.20","target":"default","tag_prefix":"","area_scope":[],"commits":[{"sha":"698347d856f9af54c08f0187aab8e467c7910a30","title":"fix task execution visibility and remove prompt directions (#1278)","files":[".lf/directions/conductor.md",".lf/directions/improviser.md",".lf/directions/listener.md",".lf/directions/macos-terminal.md",".lf/directions/testing.md",".lf/skills/xor-route.md","PROMPTS.md","README.md","TESTING.md","docs/architecture/execution.md","docs/authoring.md","docs/config.md","docs/getting-started.md","docs/index.md","docs/lf.md","docs/troubleshooting.md","rust/loopflow/build.rs","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lf-prompt.rs","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lf.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/LOOPFLOW.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/loopflow-validate.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/project/skill/project_operate.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/gate.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/prompt.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/config.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/error.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/execution.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/launch.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/prompt.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/activity.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/install.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/run.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/runs.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/top.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/usage.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/waves.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/work_catalog.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/discovery.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/output.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/rebase.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/run.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task_actions.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task_execution.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite.rs","rust/loopflow/src/trace.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/config_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/context_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/discovery_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/flow_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/golden_prompt.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/task_initialization_tests.rs","swift/Loopflow/Models/WaveWorkMap.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/MockWaveFixture.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/RegistryQueryTests.swift","tests/fixtures/dto/README.md","tests/fixtures/dto/roadmap_snapshot.json","tests/fixtures/dto/task_condition_states.json","tests/fixtures/dto/task_execution.json","tests/fixtures/dto/wave_detail.json","tests/goldens/basic.md","tests/goldens/basic.yaml","tests/goldens/builtin_debug.md","tests/goldens/builtin_debug.yaml","tests/goldens/builtin_implement.md","tests/goldens/builtin_implement.yaml","tests/goldens/builtin_review_slice.md","tests/goldens/builtin_review_slice.yaml","tests/goldens/update_goldens.py","tests/goldens/with_direction.md","tests/goldens/with_direction.yaml","tests/goldens/with_docs.md","tests/goldens/with_docs.yaml","tests/parity/fixtures/with_direction/.lf/directions/thorough.md","tests/parity/fixtures/with_direction/.lf/skills/test.md","wave/infrastructure/MEMORY.md","wave/intelligence/MEMORY.md","wave/product/MEMORY.md","website/main.py"]},{"sha":"c92a19c51c7e9517cf7c14a99307f1a65494161c","title":"cli: make installation and machine commands independent of repositories (#1280)","files":[".lf/skills/repository-context-check.md","README.md","TESTING.md","docs/architecture-reference.md","docs/lf.md","python/tests/test_checkout_refresh.py","python/tests/test_install_script.py","python/tests/test_release_automation.py","release/README.md","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lf.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/home.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/install.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/install/published.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/list.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/ops/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/profile.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/refresh.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/run.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/session.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/waves.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/machine_install.rs","rust/loopflow/src/repo.rs","rust/loopflow/src/repository.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/global_commands.rs","scripts/install.py","scripts/pull-local-bin.sh","tests/e2e/install_bootstrap.py","wave/infrastructure/MEMORY.md"]},{"sha":"7559f3189be935a7f43fdcb83f8c151f1db6a308","title":"Keep Task PRs clear about their change and merge outcome (#1282)","files":[".lf/prs-and-tasks.md","PROMPTS.md","TESTING.md","docs/lf.md","docs/waves.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/loopflow.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/pr-land.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/pr-message.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/pr-publish.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/pr-submit.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/start-chapter.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/project/skill/project_operate.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/project/skill/project_start-chapter.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/surfaces/chat.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/design.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/gate.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/kickoff.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/launch-plan.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/prompt.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/task_clarify.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/assess.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/scan.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/update-wave.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/wave-report.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/wave_operate.md","rust/loopflow/src/ops/land.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pr.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/release.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/land_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/pr_tests.rs"]},{"sha":"236086c946dfef0c9c44c090aea7821da7102aa2","title":"waves: replace project selection with resumable chapters (#1281)","files":[".lf/directions/wave-chapters.md",".lf/skills/ci-proof.md","README.md","STYLE.md","TESTING.md","docs/agent-api.md","docs/architecture-reference.md","docs/architecture.html","docs/architecture.md","docs/architecture/codebase.md","docs/architecture/execution.md","docs/architecture/planning.md","docs/conducting.md","docs/getting-started.md","docs/index.md","docs/lf.md","docs/troubleshooting.md","docs/waves.md","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lf.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/task/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/metrics.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/registry.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/server.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/LOOPFLOW.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/init.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/loopflow.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/review-chapter.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/start-chapter.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/project/flow/project-promote.yaml","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/project/flow/project.yaml","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/project/skill/project-promote.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/project/skill/project_operate.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/project/skill/project_review-chapter.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/project/skill/project_start-chapter.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/design.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/gate.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/kickoff.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/launch-plan.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/prompt.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/review-design.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/task_clarify.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/task_mutate.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/task_pursue.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/goal/ship-roadmap.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/mutate.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/review-open-work.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/scan.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/split-wave.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/update-wave.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/wave-report.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/wave_operate.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/wave_review-chapter.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/wave_start-chapter.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/process.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/ops/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/waves.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/chapter.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/chapter_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/human_session.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/metrics.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm/oauth_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/project.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/run.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task_pm.rs","rust/loopflow/src/pm/linear.rs","rust/loopflow/src/pm/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/chapters.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/children.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations/drafts/wave_chapters__34ae9954950dea7dda43fbffd4e50bdd.sql","rust/loopflow/src/store/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite/chapters.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite/children.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite/durable.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite/metrics.rs","rust/loopflow/src/work/chapter.rs","rust/loopflow/src/work/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/work/task/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/work/wave/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/discovery_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/dto_fixtures.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/repository_team_matrix.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/status_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/support/chapter.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/support/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/task_initialization_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/wave_live_smoke.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/wave_resolution_matrix.rs","scripts/loopflow-dev.py","scripts/prove_product_wave_surface.sh","swift/Loopflow/Models/ChapterHistory.swift","swift/Loopflow/Models/MetricPortfolio.swift","swift/Loopflow/Models/NowProjection.swift","swift/Loopflow/Models/SessionRecord.swift"]},{"sha":"3bdd438eb9f0e071f12288af8507a41005909845","title":"install: preserve legacy upgrades and pin release downloads (#1284)","files":[".lf/skills/compress.md","python/tests/test_shell_installer.py","release/README.md","release/install.sh","scripts/install.py"]}],"merged_prs":[{"number":1278,"title":"fix task execution visibility and remove prompt directions","body":"## Evaluate\n\n```bash\ncargo nextest run -p loopflow --lib \\\n  -E 'test(ops::task_execution::) | test(ops::task_actions::) | test(task_condition_uses_execution_evidence) | test(task_run_drill_includes_named_workers) | test(shared_project_names) | test(observation_reads_identity)' \\\n  --no-fail-fast\ncargo test -p loopflow --test context_tests --test golden_prompt\n```\n\nVerify that active or uncertain execution suppresses duplicate implementation recommendations, worker evidence takes precedence over dirty files, and Task history finds both named workers and internal-ID helpers after a Project rename. Context and golden tests check prompt assembly after direction removal. These are suggested checks; they were not run while generating this description.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nA Task marked `ready` can still have a live worker, and filtering Runs by display labels can hide independent helpers. Those gaps can lead operators or supervising agents to start duplicate implementation. This change exposes execution separately from lifecycle and resolves Run ownership consistently. It also removes the prompt-direction feature and its assembly machinery, reducing the configuration and authoring surface.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added execution state, reason, current step, worker Run, and recent Run history to Task status. Wave conditions, roadmap recommendations, and Task actions use the same execution evidence.\n- Unified Work identity lookup across Runs, Usage, Activity, and Top. Public identifiers, internal IDs, and external IDs resolve through a read-only identity query; new bound Runs record their ancestry.\n- Removed directions from CLI flags, configuration, Skill/Flow parsing, discovery, build generation, and prompt injection. Simplified gathering and rendering to `PromptComponents` and `String`.\n- Updated docs and fixtures, preserved boundary-testing guidance in `TESTING.md`, and removed the redundant runtime routing-project field from Rust and Swift.\n\n## Risks / Not included\n\n- Direction flags and injection are removed without a compatibility path. Historical direction trace records remain readable.\n- Execution describes the Task Flow; idle does not establish that independent helpers or interactive Sessions have stopped. Recent Run history is limited to 50 Runs started within seven days.\n- This does not add a launch lock, implement the Task Watch UI, or prove compatibility with an older installed execution schema.","files":[],"additions":1098,"deletions":2166,"changed_files":86,"merge_commit":"698347d856f9af54c08f0187aab8e467c7910a30"},{"number":1280,"title":"cli: make installation and machine commands independent of repositories","body":"## Evaluate\n\n```bash\ncargo test -p loopflow --test wave_resolution_tests --test wave_resolution_matrix --test global_commands\ncargo test -p loopflow --lib lf::commands::install::published::tests\ncargo test -p loopflow --lib machine_install::tests\n```\n\nThese checks cover commands without Git, repository-scoped catalogs and Wave listings, cached PM reads from registered directories, installer checksum rejection, artifact completeness, and first-install recovery.\n\nFor installation through the real CLI and shell installer, follow the disposable Ubuntu container setup in `TESTING.md`, then run inside that container:\n\n```bash\nuv run --no-project --python 3.14 /fixture/install_bootstrap.py\n```\n\nExpect fresh installation, repeat installation without asset downloads, missing-daemon repair, dirty-checkout preservation, and recovery after forced activation failure. Release transport is simulated with local HTTPS. These are evaluation commands, not a claim of a current-head test pass.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nUpdating Loopflow previously depended on a source checkout and also refreshed Git state, packages, and the Python environment. Users can now update the installed release from any directory, while `lf rebase` retains responsibility for checkout updates. Machine commands likewise use repository context only where their behavior needs it.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added a native published-release selector that pins the release tag, verifies the shell installer, and uses the existing promotion transaction. Complete installations skip asset downloads; stale or missing artifacts trigger repair.\n- Extended promotion and recovery to handle first installation without a prior selection or published fallback.\n- Removed repository requirements and journal capture from machine commands and catalog inspection. Listings retain checkout scope inside repositories and show machine-wide records outside; genuine Git failures still surface.\n- Changed macOS scheduled updates to login plus weekly by default, with positional `daily`, `hourly`, and `5min` options and no source-checkout dependency.\n- Removed the Python refresh command and shell wrapper, documented the external-installer upgrade path for older CLIs, and added focused regression and bootstrap coverage.\n\n## Risks / Not included\n\n- Automatic scheduling remains macOS-only; existing jobs need `lf install schedule` rerun to adopt the new configuration.\n- Public release-channel installation, real macOS app activation, and migration of populated historical Homes remain separate validation requirements.","files":[],"additions":1548,"deletions":919,"changed_files":31,"merge_commit":"c92a19c51c7e9517cf7c14a99307f1a65494161c"},{"number":1281,"title":"waves: replace project selection with resumable chapters","body":"## Evaluate\n\n```bash\nuv run python scripts/materialize_rust_tests.py -- cargo test -p loopflow chapter\ncargo test -p loopflow --test status_tests --test dto_fixtures\nswift test --package-path swift --filter RegistryQueryTests\nuv run python scripts/check_architecture.py\n```\n\n- Chapter tests exercise preview, interrupted transfers, lost provider responses, and retries. Started Tasks retain execution state; untouched backlog is abandoned; uncertain evidence remains unresolved.\n- Status and DTO tests cover the current chapter and direct Task listing. Swift query tests cover chapter reads and unavailable evidence.\n- Closed chapter assertions verify that later Task completion or instrument changes cannot rewrite dated history.\n\nThese are review commands; they were not run while preparing this description.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nA Wave can replace its plan without losing work already underway or carrying untouched backlog indefinitely. One current chapter makes priorities visible directly beside Tasks, while preserved history keeps previous KRs, targets, and outcomes inspectable.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added chapter creation, preview, plan updates, and history reads backed by durable transition receipts. Retries reconcile provider mutations, omitted membership, and archival by stable identity.\n- Coordinated Task retirement with worker claims in SQLite and retained first-start evidence across Flow resets. Transfers preserve Task identity, worktree, PR, and Flow state.\n- Moved reusable metric instruments to Waves and targets into chapter plans. Rotation freezes predecessor readings and evaluation dates; untargeted readings retain values without pass/fail judgments.\n- Replaced ordinary Project selection and operation with Wave → Task navigation across CLI, desktop, builtins, and documentation. Added chapter history and explicit unavailable/stale states.\n\n## Risks / Not included\n\nThis changes CLI commands, JSON shapes, and metric authoring. Rust and Swift consumers must move together. Rotation mutates Linear membership, cancels untouched backlog, and archives predecessor Projects; missing or conflicting evidence can leave a transition pending reconciliation.","files":[],"additions":7142,"deletions":7715,"changed_files":144,"merge_commit":"236086c946dfef0c9c44c090aea7821da7102aa2"},{"number":1282,"title":"Keep Task PRs clear about their change and merge outcome","body":"## Evaluate\n\nSuggested walkthrough (not performed against live GitHub): publish a Task PR\nwith a title and opening paragraph describing its specific change. The title\nand summary should remain intact, followed by one Task note. Refresh the same\narmed head: the note should still describe its existing merge consequence.\nPublish a changed head: the note should show that no settlement is requested.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nTask PR titles previously repeated the broader Task name, and managed metadata\npreceded the author's summary. Reviewers can now read what this increment\ndelivers first, then see its Task and merge consequence without reconstructing\nexecution history.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Preserve authored titles and summaries while replacing one managed Task\n  note. Read existing settlement under the mutation lock for the published head.\n- Carry title and body together through parsing, rendering, and landing;\n  retain override, cache, local-landing, and release re-arm behavior.\n- Align writing skills around Task problems, design decisions, and delivered\n  PR benefits. Keep automated evidence separate from user walkthroughs and use\n  readable links in reports.\n- Document how to stage an existing design in the prepared Task worktree before\n  running the selected Flow. Correct reporting guidance for the different\n  active-PR shapes returned by status and roadmap.\n\n## Checks\n\n- 55 focused Rust unit checks passed; all 15 builtin contracts passed again\n  after correcting reporting guidance.\n- 96 publication, landing, release, and prompt-golden checks passed:\n  `cargo nextest run -p loopflow --test pr_tests --test land_tests --test release_tests --test golden_prompt --build-jobs 4 --test-threads 4`.\n- Website: 78 passed, 3 existing skips. Architecture, formatting, and Clippy\n  passed.\n- Copy reduction: 42 Rust lines added, 99 removed (57 net removed).\n\n## Risks / Not included\n\nProvider integration checks use temporary repositories and mocked responses.\nNo live publication, human reader study, or live design handoff was performed.\nAutomatic scratch transfer and checkout adoption remain outside this change.\nThe aggregate local gate is blocked by the active main checkout's build budget;\nfull Rust and cross-platform coverage remains with CI.\n","files":[],"additions":1039,"deletions":394,"changed_files":32,"merge_commit":"7559f3189be935a7f43fdcb83f8c151f1db6a308"},{"number":1284,"title":"install: preserve legacy upgrades and pin release downloads","body":"```bash\nlf install\n```\n\nOlder installed CLIs update main and then invoke `scripts/install.py refresh`. Removing that entry point stranded their upgrades. Keep it as a hidden delegate to the existing release installer, preserving install-directory overrides and failure reporting.\n\nResolve the latest tag from the GitHub release page before downloading assets. Asset redirects end at GitHub's CDN and cannot supply the tag; the previous fixture concealed that failure.\n\nValidation: 27 installer tests pass, including legacy invocation, explicit/environment install paths, and preservation of existing binaries on download or checksum failure. Ruff and diff checks pass. The repaired entry point completed a real published v0.12.20 CLI, daemon, and Mac app installation. Plain `lf install` requires this fix on main; replay it after merge.","files":[],"additions":121,"deletions":36,"changed_files":5,"merge_commit":"3bdd438eb9f0e071f12288af8507a41005909845"}],"decisions":null,"previous_release_notes":"# v0.12.20\n\n<!-- loopflow:release-notes=narrative;gate=safe -->\n\nv0.12.20 makes Task progress and direction recoverable across worker exits. Tasks advance through saved Flow positions, corrections live in Linear comments, and Run conclusions remain available for later review. Checkout refresh and Linear credential recovery also improve, reducing the manual work needed to keep unattended execution moving.\n\n## Resume Tasks from saved progress\n\nEach Task now runs one persisted Flow invocation. A worker advances one saved boundary and launches its successor when autonomous work remains, so progress no longer depends on a resident controller's conversation history.\n\n- Interrupted work resumes at its saved position; stale workers and human decisions cannot advance a replacement invocation.\n- Active invocations retain their selected Flow and Skill definitions when those definitions are edited later.\n- Human approval, iteration, and resumable sessions remain tied to the invocation they concern. Independent Task-bound Runs provide context without advancing the Flow.\n- Projects operate through finite Runs and recommend one Task Flow. Use `lf task run --flow` to override that recommendation.\n\n## Keep Task corrections in one place\n\nDirection entered on a Linear issue or through `lf task steer` now shares one authored comment history. Only the worker advancing that Task consumes it, keeping corrections scoped to the intended execution.\n\n- Posting direction leaves an idle Task idle and does not inject steering into independent Task-bound Runs.\n- Workers refresh comments before Skill execution and while running. Polling and webhooks reconcile comment edits without duplicate delivery.\n- Run traces distinguish direction included in the starting prompt from direction accepted by a live provider; neither proves that the model followed it.\n- The Mac Wave composer offers **Send** for text and **Interrupt** for an active turn when the composer is empty.\n\n## Catch up without losing local work\n\n`lf rebase` on stale main now updates HEAD after fetching upstream. Rebase from a sibling refreshes canonical main before integrating the caller, using the same preserving updater as install and ordinary worktree refresh.\n\n- Main updates retain unpublished commit identities and staged, working, and untracked edits. Creating the next sibling also preserves main's unpublished commits.\n- `lf install` updates main, required tools, the Python environment, and the published release. Complete, current installations skip downloads; missing or damaged Mac app bundles still reach the installer.\n- Linear authentication refresh serializes credential exchanges and persists complete rotated pairs without overwriting a newer reconnect or deletion. Temporary failures allow one bounded retry; unrecoverable failures distinguish retry from reconnect.\n\n## Recover the evidence behind a review\n\nChapter reviews now preserve the accepted planning boundary and reconcile KR verdicts against recorded evidence. Missing evidence stays explicit, and later reviews use the newest merged chapter-start record.\n\n- `lf runs --parent <run-id> --json` discovers direct child Runs without the usual history cap.\n- `lf runs <run-id> --final` retrieves durable conclusions. Older Runs fall back to labeled streamed prose, which may include commentary.\n- The archived baseline and accepted plan preserve decisions and receipts; they do not establish that planned improvements or KRs have been achieved.\n\n## Operational notes\n\n- Migrate automation using `--first`, `--loop`, `--finally`, or removed Project process controls to the persisted Flow model. Legacy positions that cannot reconstruct a complete invocation require explicit restart; available Work and human-session facts are preserved.\n- Generic Work and Project steering, `lf chat --steer`, and Wave live steering are removed. Pass Project and Wave guidance as instructions to their operate skills. Task direction publication and comment refresh before a Skill require Linear availability; bare Task interrupts remain local.\n- Finishing a Flow does not complete its Task or select another Flow. Delivery and Task completion remain explicit. `ci-fix` now owns rebase, verification, publication, and auto-merge; the landing watcher blocks on unchanged or unarmed repairs.\n- After upgrading, run `lf install schedule` to enable login/hourly macOS refresh. Scheduler validation used simulated plist/reload checks; live scheduled firing and wake recovery remain unverified in the included evidence.\n- OAuth expiry and rejection recovery were exercised against simulated HTTPS in a development Home. Live candidate recovery against Linear and sustained operational reliability remain unverified.\n\n## Small changes\n\n- Codex final-answer receipts avoid repeating streamed text in chat rendering.\n- Architecture checks exclude frozen chapter evidence while continuing to check live instructions.","source_limits":{"context_bytes":131072,"commits":256,"merged_prs":200,"files_per_change":100,"area_scopes":32,"name_bytes":256,"title_bytes":300,"path_bytes":512,"pr_body_bytes":4096,"decisions_bytes":16384,"previous_release_notes_bytes":16384,"release_notes_bytes":61440},"omissions":{"commits":0,"merged_prs":0,"commit_files":44,"pr_files":0,"area_scopes":0,"text_bytes":0,"decisions_bytes":0,"previous_release_notes_bytes":0}}